WEBVTT

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.970
The Song of Depravity

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.440
That weapon was pretty scary.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.980
<i>I've never seen anything so big before.</i>

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.740
<i>What if it transforms?</i>

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.490
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.700
I wonder where it went.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.540
If it crosses the checkpoint to the west,
then that means

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.160
it's going to the front line
near the border.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.120
The front line?

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.210
There really is going to be a war.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.180
In any case, that weapon just now

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.680
and the Minstrel Hunt...

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.010
The Capital Army will do anything
to achieve their goals.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.060
You said you wanted to go
to the Capital, right?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.730
You'd better forget about it.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.940
It's too dangerous to go now.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.770
But...

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.610
I'm going anyway. I'm going to sing
with the Court Orchestra.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.240
The Capital Army is after
the power of your songs.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.870
I'm going to sing my heart out
to that star.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.040
Then sing at the Star Song Festival.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.590
Singing to the stars will make
your wishes come true.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.590
-Hey, you.
-I promised!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:44.140
I promised someone I love that I'm going
to make my dream come true.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.390
That's all...

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.310
I have left.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.480
I understand.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.820
I'm going to find a carriage.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.900
It's a long way to the Capital.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.240
What?! You'll come with us?

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.410
I'm betting on you. And...

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.490
I like your songs, Rin.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.710
Hey, hey! That makes you
the first member of my orchestra!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.330
Rin's Orchestra?

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.500
Well, I don't mind.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.540
Great!

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.930
What's going on this time?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.650
Look! There are some girls over there!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.870
Frontline unit, march forward!

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.470
Oh, sorry. Aren't you that rich kid
from the Leobolt family? You're too frail.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.680
I heard you were removed
as the songstress's guard.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:08.930
Serves you right.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.140
The frontline unit is just a group
of pawns sent to die.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.650
Did you remember to say bye to your mama?

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.280
Henry...

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.620
Are you ready?

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.120
Yes.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.920
Once the frontline unit leaves,
we're leaving, too.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.130
If they get injured in battle,

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:42.920
you'll revive them again and again
with the power of your songs.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.010
I understand.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.070
They're transporting parts for the weapon.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.570
Who are those girls?

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:08.530
They're Rhythm Masters.
They raise the morale of the troops

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.410
and increase their productivity.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.870
They're different
from the Court Orchestra?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:14.910
Yeah.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.290
Rhythm Masters are military personnel
belonging to the Capital Army.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.460
Those girls are military personnel?

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.090
You're right. This is unusual.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:27.510
Why are there young children
in the Capital Army?

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.970
Right. They should just escape
from the army.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.180
They look so bored.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:37.770
If escaping from the army was easy,
they wouldn't have such a hard time--

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.480
They escaped!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.810
What?! It's going to hit the ground!

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.190
Are you okay?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.160
What is this creature?

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.790
This creature...
It's scientifically impossible!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.920
She's asleep.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.840
I don't even know what to say.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.460
Hey! Monica!

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:12.640
There you are!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.310
What in the world is going on?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.980
Hey, you've got a nice sword.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.570
It's been passed down
in the Leobolt family, right?

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:32.410
They say that it never rusts or breaks,
no matter what.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:38.080
A sword like that is wasted
on a rich kid like you. Ow!

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.080
Don't touch it.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.870
Ow. Let go of me! Damn.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.420
Can't you take a joke?

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.170
Hey! I said it was a joke!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:49.840
What...?

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:50.840
It's the enemy!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:57.260
Get ready for a real battle, rich kid.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.860
Sorry.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:09.150
She has a habit of falling asleep
when in danger.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.860
-What kind of a habit is that?
-Monica, wake up! It's morning already!

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.950
Allu... Good morning.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:23.000
She woke up like it was
any other morning...

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.710
-Beast.
-You're awfully rude.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.670
Anyway, are you Rhythm Masters
from the Capital Army?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.670
Yeah, that's right. Who are you?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.510
We're Rin's Orchestra.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.970
I'm not a member of the Orchestra.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.680
So, that means you're an Orchestra of two.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:41.810
That's hilarious.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.770
We may be just two now,

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.900
but someday we'll be a big orchestra
in the Capital!

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.400
An orchestra in the Capital?

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:55.360
-It's not that easy.
-We'll work hard to make it happen.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.780
No way. Just give up.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.660
You're so mean. You're the one
who should stop making weapons.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.580
And what do you know?

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.420
This is our job!

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.170
This is something... necessary for us!

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.590
There's no way that weapons
or war are ever necessary!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:16.590
Shut up!

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:18.600
-What do you--?
-Allu.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.560
Let's go, Monica.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:33.360
-I'm so angry. And I'm hungry now, too.
-How is that relevant?

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.200
I bet they're crossing the checkpoint
in the west with that weapon.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.660
With the Minstrel Hunt going on,

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.540
we'll have to detour around the mountains
to get to the Capital.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.090
Let's get going.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.680
Is this a piece of the cargo?

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.520
General Bazra, a message from the prince.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.230
What is it?

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:09.520
Sir, I'll relay his message
using his exact words.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.820
"Fighting has already begun
at the front line.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.110
Why isn't the general here?

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:17.280
Tell him to report to me at once."

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:21.570
I'm afraid I won't be able
to report back to him.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.540
What do you mean?

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.210
Because the messenger is going to die.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.420
What--?

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:40.800
The stars are particularly
beautiful tonight.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.970
Finis.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.400
Here we go! A royal straight shining!

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:54.360
How about that?

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.320
Too bad. I've got a five body.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.030
Thanks.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.490
No way.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:03.700
You're cheating.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.830
Excited over a royal?

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.920
Hey! I'll take another glass of ale!
And lemonade for the kids.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.420
You seem pretty happy.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.880
Because I won.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.340
How do you like our food?

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:23.680
It's great!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.270
I'm glad. It looks like life isn't easy
for you either.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.180
You're still so young,
but with two kids...

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.900
No, they're not my kids. And I'm single.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.310
Oh, really?

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.480
Can't you tell?

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:40.320
Sorry. I'm blind.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.910
I'm sorry for being rude.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:45.160
But I have good hearing.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.410
So, I could tell that you're young.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.370
Right. I have daughters, too.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.420
They're probably around your age.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.540
What are they like?

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:59.960
They said they went to the Capital
and joined the Court Orchestra.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.220
Amazing, right?

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.680
That's so nice!

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:08.140
I hope I can listen
to them play music soon.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.430
I'm looking forward
to when they come home.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:26.200
Hey.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.740
Calm down! We're done here.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.960
Hey. All these guys over here...

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.510
This isn't the work of that rich kid,
is it?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:43.930
Who knows?

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:46.890
Hey, are you leaving the wounded behind?

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.970
And what if I am?

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.430
We can still save them with treatment.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:54.730
-We should wait for the medical unit--
-There's no need.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.310
You bastard... They're your comrades.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:01.820
The wounded will be healed
by the songstress who's coming later.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.280
With the power of songs.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.360
Finis is--?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.830
So, now we're an immortal army.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.410
No way...

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.160
She can't...

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.790
If she sings again, her life will be...

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:19.000
in danger.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.890
Hey. Get into formation!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.140
All recovered! Let's catch up
to the frontline unit!

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:38.900
Yeah!

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.230
Miss Finis!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.860
Good work, Finis.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.450
I hope that...

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.530
the war ends soon.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.830
About that...

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.000
The soldiers in our Capital Army fight
and get wounded.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.170
Then they get healed
by the power of songs and fight again.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.130
Don't you think it's inefficient?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.920
I have a good idea.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:11.220
Taking a detour would mean

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:14.310
that we'd be moving farther away
from the Capital in the south.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:17.560
I know it's a pain,
but when we pass the checkpoint,

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:19.900
the road to the Capital will open up.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.270
I see...

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:26.530
-Those girls from yesterday!
-What are you doing here?

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.860
I was about to say the same thing!

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.370
We're regulars here.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.490
We came here yesterday for the first time.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.660
Is that you, Allu?

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:38.790
Mom!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.290
Allu, you're back!

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.710
Is Monica with you?

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:45.800
I'm here!

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.260
Welcome home, Monica. How was the Capital?

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.760
It's hard to manage it all.
We perform every day. We're exhausted.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:56.390
Hold on--

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:59.020
It isn't easy being
in the Court Orchestra.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:02.810
But when things calm down a bit,
we'll invite you to the Capital.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.530
Thank you.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:14.910
<i>Liar.</i>

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.200
So, who said they were
in the Court Orchestra?

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.870
Go ahead and laugh if you want.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.080
Why did you lie about it?

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.000
It's not a lie.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.800
We really are in the Court Orchestra!

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:31.720
Monica!

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.140
Is she doing that on purpose?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.690
No. That is her best.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.480
Al, bring her back in a stylish way.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:45.480
What kind of order is that?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.730
I can't do that.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:48.730
Al.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:49.900
<i>Be a man.</i>

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.990
<i>-Be a man.</i>
<i>-Be a man.</i>

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.870
<i>-Be a man.</i>
-Knock it off with that weird chant.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.780
<i>-Be a man.</i>
<i>-Be a man.</i>

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.290
<i>-Be a man.</i>
-Okay, I got it.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.470
Um... Why are we here?

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.840
Do you see that, Finis?

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:18.140
That's the enemy's camp.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.520
Well, then,

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:23.600
could you end this battle for us?

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.060
Why are you surprised? It's simple.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:30.320
You could use fire, a blizzard,
or even water.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.900
Create a miracle with your songs.

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:36.240
Massacre the enemy.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:40.500
Sorry.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.660
Your name's Rin, right?

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.580
Sorry for saying mean things to you.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:50.050
No, it's okay. What did she mean
when she said it wasn't a lie?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.930
We love music, too.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:03.180
Our dream was to join the Court Orchestra.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.610
My little sister is a genius
at mimicking things.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.940
She can master
any song she listens to once.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.400
Really?

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:17.660
Then why did you give up your dream
to be a part of the Capital Army?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:19.910
We need money.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.370
<i>We have to buy special medicine</i>

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.420
<i>to heal our mom's eyes.</i>

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.460
<i>But we don't have enough money.</i>

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:34.970
<i>If we followed our dream, we'd run</i>
<i>out of time to stop the disease.</i>

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.720
<i>So, we thought it would be better</i>
<i>to become Rhythm Masters,</i>

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.430
<i>to earn money quickly.</i>

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:47.310
<i>Even if that meant joining</i>
<i>the Capital Army.</i>

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.280
So, you lied about being
in the Court Orchestra

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.820
to stop your mother from worrying.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:03.240
We don't like creating tools for war.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.710
But as long as our mom gets better,

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.790
that's enough for us.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:12.300
Then just make that lie come true.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:18.300
Your mother said she wanted
to hear your music.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:21.390
Not that music you were playing
with a bored look on your face!

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.770
-If we could, we wouldn't be having--
-You can!

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:28.440
Form an orchestra with us.
Let's go to the Capital together!

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:32.610
We'll take the Court Orchestra with us
and sing at the Star Song Festival!

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:35.190
That's impossible!

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:38.030
-Miracles like that don't happen!
-Miracles...

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:40.360
can come true.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:44.240
I can't do that.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.830
To kill people with the power of my songs?

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:52.460
That's too bad.
I thought it was a good idea.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.920
Well, it can't be helped.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:05.180
<i>A song</i>

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:09.810
<i>That awakens and calls</i>

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:14.110
<i>People repeat the song</i>

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:17.820
<i>In their hearts</i>

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.070
I have a message!

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.820
Miss Finis will no longer sing
the Song of Healing!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.330
Instead, she's going to use the Weapon
of Song to annihilate the enemy!

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:27.160
<i>I wish to shine love</i>
<i>into the sky</i>

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.160
Weapon...

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.790
of Song?

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.040
<i>from which the light has disappeared</i>

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:42.470
<i>On the journey</i>

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:45.720
<i>Of no end</i>

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:48.810
The enemy camp before us
will soon be annihilated

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.690
with the power of the songs of Miss Finis,
the Human Weapon!

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.440
<i>Everyone is searching</i>

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.520
What is he saying?

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.070
What's going on?

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:58.690
<i>For the meaning of this life</i>

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.280
Hey. Where are you going?

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:06.120
<i>The world</i>

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.370
<i>Is a gentle ship</i>

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.080
<i>It sways</i>

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.250
<i>And gets swayed</i>

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:20.590
<i>It envelops</i><i>everything</i>

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:25.390
There's no way that she-- That Finis
would use the power of songs for war.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.720
<i>and embraces everyone the way they are</i>

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:33.690
<i>The world</i><i>is a ship of hope</i>

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:39.360
<i>It sways</i><i>and gets swayed</i>

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.110
<i>It carries</i>

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:42.320
This can't be.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.820
<i>People's sadness</i>

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.820
This can't be happening!

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.290
<i>I can see.</i>

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:53.790
I can see.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.250
I can see...

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.630
the two of you!

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:01.590
Mom...

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:04.180
Thank you!

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:05.260
Mom!

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:09.760
Sorry for everything until now.
I'm fine now.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.730
Thank you...

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:16.400
from the bottom of my heart.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:24.650
I'll ask you again.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:27.240
Are you really coming with us?

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.240
Of course.

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:31.990
We discovered the type of music
that we really want to play.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.960
Rin, thanks.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:36.540
I like you.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.420
Your songs cheer people up.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.550
Your songs are miracles.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:52.560
Here we go! Let's shoot
for the Capital together!

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.560
Yeah!

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:56.980
I can't believe
that she even gave us a carriage.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:58.400
Your mother is so nice.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:03.900
Rin!

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:06.200
That man... Mr. Leobolt?!

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:20.540
Demon.
